            <div xml:id="d65">

                <pb facs="0192" n="96" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg96"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89France/319: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-06-09T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 9, 1926—1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>166. Your 232, June 8, 4 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Department entirely approves your action in warning the French that no
                        reservations would be accepted.</item>
                    <pb facs="0193" n="97" xml:id="pg97"/>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Should you be asked to forward any reservations, I suggest that you might
                        refuse on ground that to comply with request would, in your opinion, result
                        only in rebuff.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
